    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "此"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "この／これ"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Standalone connective/determiner 此 ('this / the said') printed between the 延高 sub-figure and the 現石 column, introducing the current-koku figure. A real, solid black printed glyph (x1653-1712, y1179-1240) — the proposal wrongly dismissed this band as facing-page bleed-through because its row-projection only scanned y1300+ and missed the glyph at y1179-1240. Structural marker, not a data value (analogous to the unboxed 内 markers)."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "此連接"
      }
